## Problem (tree truth)
| Fact | Evidence |
|------|----------|
| Sprint pin | `SPRINT.oot` R2 ACTIVE: multi-import type check in `ooda/oodac/` |
| PM plain words | `PM.oot`: one file checks ok; **many files in one build still fails** |
| Tiny multi works | `bootstrap/corpus/import/pass/multi_ok.oo` + `import_load_smoke.oo` — in-tree load + check OK |
| Scale residual | `AUDIT_RESIDUAL.oot` **R4/R5**: full expanded `check` on oodac-scale trees times out / hangs; `PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1` common |
| Concat path | `load_import.oo` DFS expands imports into **one** source stream; `check_drive.oo` typechecks expanded string (1 MiB cap) |
| Issue #9 | Expanded-stream LINE:COL, not per-file local — residual named in `load_import.oo`, `tc_diag.oo`, `DIAG_CODES.oot`, `typecheck_line_smoke.oo` |
| Modular scaffold (half-landed) | `check_mod.oo` has `run_check_module_body` but **`run_check_path` still full-concat** + tree cache only |
| Signature hook | `tc_names.oo` `typecheck_undefined_vars_ext(..., extra_binds)` — pre-seed external names; product path still calls plain `typecheck_undefined_vars` |
| External script | `scripts/oodac_module_check.oo` — per-module stubs + unit check (avoids OOM); **not** product `oodac check` path |
| Cache API | `check_cache.oo`: `m_` mod keys + `t_` tree keys; product uses **t_ only** on full expanded hash (`check_mod.oo`) |
| Collect graph | `check_collect.oo` `collect_module_paths` + `strip_import_lines` exist — ready for modular driver |

**Not this wave:** full multi-module IR, parallel typechecker rewrite, emit-c graph redesign, DESIGN moonshots.

## Constraints (hard)
1. **Path A only** — fail-closed residual, not “perfect multi-module TC.”
2. **Reuse scaffolds** — prefer wiring `check_mod` / `check_collect` / `extra_binds` over new architecture.
3. **Honesty** — no cache greenwash; no claim per-file LINE fixed unless smoke proves it.
4. **Immune tests** — pass + fail fixtures; tiny multi stays green; large-tree path must not soft-OK on skip.
5. **Line pressure** — ≤256 owned files; small DE land, not fairy code.
6. **Fairy writes ideas only** — Domain Experts own implement + prove.

## Darwin scorecard (path-A residual)
Axes 0–10 (higher = survives compile cycle). Sum/5 ≈ rank:

| Axis | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Close** | Moves R2 residual (scale fail / multi-file TC / Issue #9) |
| **Honest** | Named residual; no greenwash cache or LINE lies |
| **Smoke** | Cheap pass+fail shapes; hooks existing import/typecheck rails |
| **Entropy** | Lowers \(S\) (untested claims, fail-open, hand-waves, oversize) |
| **Ship** | ≤ few small files + smoke; uses existing hooks |

**Rule:** losers pruned. 1–2 winners advance to DE this sprint turn.

